  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What the browser proves",
      "items": [
        "Panel: one interactive element (the settings gear) and zero extra focusable nodes once a real gear click records open_settings",
        "Settings: the seven h2 sections in order, one main shell, zero iframes",
        "WebGL 2.0 via unmasked ANGLE Metal (gl.getError() == 0); sampled 13.48 fps idle at job_load 0 and 22.47 fps at 0.9, renderCount 16 to 106"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Single source of truth",
      "items": [
        "Banned tokens, settings section order, and the panel aria-label come from desktop/src/__tests__/ui-removal-contract.test.ts",
        "That file SHA-256 is recorded in the receipt, and tests/test_jarvis_desktop_render_check.py re-derives the same expectations",
        "A missing or unparsable contract ends the run with exit 2, and restoring the pre-fix status label failed the run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Where the evidence stops",
      "items": [
        "Chromium for Testing is not the installed WebKit webview, so this is bundle evidence, not installed-app evidence",
        "The Tauri bridge is a deterministic stub; Rust-side snapshot shaping is covered by the cargo tests instead",
        "Sampled fps is headless-RAF only and is not claimed to equal the webview; no account, no network, and no live KakaoTalk send is involved"
      ]
    }
  ]
